A||||3||Philphine||cheap thrills: the stereo version||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||11-05-2000||07:48 PM||||<BR>got one piece for my cheap thrills fiero. a local wholesale to public type store (you pay 15% over cost plus tax) had some 8" infinity 3 ways for $115. they had two sets so i got them both. i'm in there a lot so the owner knocked a few $ off and i got them for $110 a set out the door. got them out of layaway and am working out how to install a set in the dead pedal area.<P>i think i was telling fropuff about a mail order place that sells soundstream cheap. it's called sound city. they have a 3 channel soundstream 2x35 and 1x70 @ 4ohm, 100@2ohm amp for $99. i think that will be what i use for this car.<P>still need a sub and stero but i think i can put in a compleat and good sounding system for $6-700. it may sound like a lot but if you're into car stereo you know thats a pretty cheap thrill. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
